===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{senseid|en|interjection}} {{lb|en|colloquial}} {{n-g|A [[holophrastic]] expression used to dismiss something that the speaker doesn't care about, doesn't think important, or doesn't want to consider or discuss any further. Sometimes conceived as an {{glossary|ellipsis}} of ''[[whatever you say]]'', implying feigned deference: ''whatever you say [apparently must be true]''.}}
#: {{syn|en|whatev|whevs|what the fuck ever|whatever you say|;|whoopee do|;|if you say so}}
#: {{nearsyn|en|meh|so what}}
#: {{ux|en|So you broke it? '''Whatever'''! Get a grip.}}
#: {{ux|en|Go brush your teeth. – '''Whatever'''!}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=Jan 1991|journal=Isaac Asimov's Science Fiction Magazine|page=66|passage="It's not silk, it's muslin." "'''Whatever'''."}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=June 3, 1998|episode=w:Conjoined Fetus Lady|title=w:South Park|season=2|number=5|passage=Yeah, '''whatever''' you old dried up fat hog.}}

====Usage notes====
* May appear rude or discourteous. Can be used to end an argument without conceding the point, implying that the issue is not worth discussing or indicating a general sense of apathy toward the subject.

